{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03NB", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\varphi : V \\to U$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}(\\varphi) : \\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{F}(V)$", "MATH_0008": "$s \\mapsto s|_V$", "MATH_0009": "$s \\mapsto \\varphi^*s$", "MATH_0010": "$s|_V$", "MATH_0011": "$\\varphi$", "MATH_0012": "$\\Gamma(U, \\mathcal{F}) = \\mathcal{F}(U)$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0014": "$W \\to V \\to U$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0016": "$s \\in \\Gamma(U, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0017": "$(s|_V)|_W = s |_W$", "MATH_0018": "$\\text{id}_U : U \\to U$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0020": "$\\textit{PSh} (\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0021": "$\\textit{PAb}\n(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{C}^{opp}$", "MATH_0023": "$\\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0024": "$\\textit{Ab}$", "MATH_0025": "$\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0026": "$\\textit{PAb}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0027": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-remark-big-categories}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0005": "\\noindent", "TEXTBFCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTBFOPEN_0001": "{\\bf ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:87afc336cddb93ffac809aa49aeb1c4879f5197ea6501822a1a7f80575f16102", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0f76b06e9e822d231c96943d113cff54afd5617ce85ff8abc6177ab6164db745", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<TEXTBFOPEN_0001>Terminology.<TEXTBFCLOSE_0001> If <MATH_0001>, then elements of\n<MATH_0002> are called <TEXTITOPEN_0001>sections<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of <MATH_0003> over\n<MATH_0004>. For <MATH_0005> in <MATH_0006>, the\nmap <MATH_0007>\nis called the <TEXTITOPEN_0002>restriction map<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> and is often denoted <MATH_0008>\nor sometimes <MATH_0009>. The notation <MATH_0010> is ambiguous\nsince the restriction map depends on <MATH_0011>, but it is a standard\nabuse of notation. We also use the notation\n<MATH_0012>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nSaying that <MATH_0013> is a functor means that if\n<MATH_0014> are morphisms in <MATH_0015> and\n<MATH_0016> then\n<MATH_0017>, with the abuse of\nnotation just seen. Moreover, the restriction mappings corresponding to\nthe identity morphisms <MATH_0018> are the identity.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nThe category of presheaves of sets (respectively of abelian presheaves) on\n<MATH_0019> is denoted <MATH_0020> (resp. <MATH_0021>). It is the category of functors from <MATH_0022> to\n<MATH_0023> (resp. <MATH_0024>), which is to say that the morphisms of\npresheaves are natural transformations of functors. We only consider the\ncategories <MATH_0025> and <MATH_0026>\nwhen the category <MATH_0027> is small. (Our convention is that a category\nis small unless otherwise mentioned, and if it isn't small it should be\nlisted in Categories, Remark <REF_0001>.)\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:beec6c7a7354e01f864b91c89972a3c59b33ed228fe987241262425d3e7f7a19", "unit_id": "tag:03NB:prose-0002"}
